```
Title: ETW Trace Evasion Activity
Author: @neu5ron, Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Jonhnathan Ribeiro, oscd.community
Date: 2019-03-22
Level: high
Description: Detects command line activity that attempts to tamper with Event Tracing for Windows (ETW) by clearing or disabling
 trace logs or providers. Adversaries may target ETW to blind security tooling and evade detection by removing
 visibility into process activity, network connections, and other telemetry sources.
 Techniques include clearing logs via wevtutil, disabling trace sessions via logman, and removing or modifying
 ETW providers using PowerShell cmdlets such as Remove-EtwTraceProvider and Set-EtwTraceProvider.
MITRE Tactic: Uncategorized
Tags: attack.stealth, attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1070, attack.t1685, car.2016-04-002
Reference: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_etw_trace_evasion.yml
```
(Image="*\\wevtutil.exe" OR OriginalFileName="wevtutil.exe" (CommandLine IN ("* cl *", "*clear-log*") CommandLine="*-Trace*" OR CommandLine="*/Trace*" OR CommandLine="*–Trace*" OR CommandLine="*—Trace*" OR CommandLine="*―Trace*") OR (CommandLine IN ("* sl *", "*set-log*") CommandLine="*-e:false*" OR CommandLine="*/e:false*" OR CommandLine="*–e:false*" OR CommandLine="*—e:false*" OR CommandLine="*―e:false*")) OR (Image="*\\logman.exe" OR OriginalFileName="Logman.exe" CommandLine="*update*" CommandLine="*trace*" CommandLine="*--p*" CommandLine="*-ets*") OR (CommandLine="*Remove-EtwTraceProvider*" OR (CommandLine="*Set-EtwTraceProvider*" CommandLine="*0x11*") OR (CommandLine="*Set-EtwTraceProvider*" CommandLine="* 17*") OR (CommandLine="*Set-EtwTraceProvider*" CommandLine="*'17'*") OR (CommandLine="*Set-EtwTraceProvider*" CommandLine="*\"17\"*") Image IN ("*\\powershell.exe", "*\\pwsh.exe") OR OriginalFileName IN ("powershell.exe", "pwsh.dll"))